## Battery services

Consistent electrical performance is what stops a truck failing to start on a
morning nobody planned for. We provide:

- Battery testing and diagnostics
- Battery replacements
- Terminal and cable inspections

## Why bring it here

A battery that will not crank is often not the battery. Our technicians measure
before they replace — static voltage, crank voltage, alternator output under
load, and parasitic draw with the ignition off — so the part that gets changed
is the part that failed. That is also what keeps a replacement from failing
early behind a fault nobody found.

Charlotte’s heat is hard on batteries: high temperatures drive electrolyte loss
and rough road surfaces work the internal plates. Testing on an interval is
worth more here than the manufacturer’s number suggests.

{% callout tone="caution" title="Replace dual batteries as a pair" %}
Most diesel trucks run a dual-battery bank. Replacing one of the two puts a new
battery in parallel with a worn one, and the new one is the one that pays for
it. Match the pair on rating and age.
{% /callout %}

